<component type="desktop-application">
 <id>io.github.dwaynebailey.Virtaal</id>
 <metadata_license>CC-BY-SA-3.0</metadata_license>
 <project_license>GPL-2.0-or-later</project_license>
 <!-- l10n: The name should be less than 30 characters -->
 <_name>Virtaal Translation Tool</_name>
 <!-- l10n: The summary should be less than 100 characters -->
 <_summary>A translation tool to help a human translator translate files into other languages</_summary>
 <description>
  <!-- l10n: Paragraphs should be less than 600 characters -->
  <_p>
    Virtaal is a program for doing translation. It aims for a delightful combination of simplicity and power. It integrates with selected online resources to make translation fun, while helping to improve translation quality.
  </_p>
  <_p>
    The initial focus is on software translation (localization or l10n), but is definitely meant to be useful as a general purpose tool for Computer Aided Translation (CAT).
  </_p>
  <_p>Some features:</_p>
  <ul>
   <!-- l10n: These list items should be less than 100 characters -->
   <_li>Translation reuse (translation memory)</_li>
   <_li>Terminology assistance</_li>
   <_li>AutoCompletor and AutoCorrector</_li>
   <_li>Quality checks with customization for many languages</_li>
  </ul>
 </description>
 <screenshots>
  <screenshot type="default">
    <image>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwaynebailey/virtaal/py3/docs/_static/appdata/welcome.png</image>
